  "report_period": "Week 21 (19th May to 26th May 2023)",
  "commentary": {
    "bulkers": "Foremost Group have committed their Capesize \"Bay May\" 178/2010 SWS, China (SS/DD 05/2025, BWTS fitted) to Far Eastern interests for USD 25,5 mill, while the one-year-older sister vessel \"Mineral Ningbo\" 178/2009 SWS, China (SS/DD 07/2024, BWTS fitted) was sold a week ago at USD 24 mill. In addition, Berge Bulk committed their \"Berge Cristobal\" 177/2003 Namura & Sasebo, Japan (SS/DD 07/2023, Scrubber fitted) to Chinese interests for low USD 13 mill. Note that a week ago, the one-year-younger \"Tasik Melati\" 180/2004 Koyo, Japan (SS/DD 05/2024, BWTS fitted) was sold at USD 15,5 mill. On the Supramax sector, the \"Ella\" 52/2003 Tsuneishi, Japan (SS/DD 11/2023, BWTS fitted) of Taylor Maritime was committed for USD 9,7 mill, while the one-year-older \"Great Wenjie\" 50/2002 Oshima, Japan (SS 09/2027, DD 09/2025, BWTS fitted) was sold for USD 7,5 mill. For reference, the \"Worldera-1\" 51/2001 Oshima, Japan (SS/DD 12/2024, BWTS fitted) was sold back in March at USD 8 mill. The Handysize \"Caribbean Spirit\" 35/2009 Nantong, China (SS/DD 07/2024, BWTS fitted) was committed for USD 10,8 mill. For comparison, the one- year-younger sister vessel \"Ithaca Stockholm\" 35/2010 Nantong, China (SS/DD 07/2025, BWTS fitted) was sold earlier this month at USD 11 mill. Moreover, German owners sold their \"Alice Star\" 32/2008 Hakodate, Japan (SS/DD 09/2023) for low USD 12 mill. Note that the one-year-younger sister vessel \"Super Gunner\" 32/2009 Hakodate, Japan (SS/DD 02/2024, BWTS fitted) was sold a week ago at USD 13 mill.",
    "tankers": "Pleiades Shipping Agents have committed their Aframax \"Sperchios\" 107/2018 Namura & Sasebo, Japan (SS/DD due, BWTS & Scrubber fitted) to Middle Eastern interests for USD 68,5 mill. Furthermore, Sea World Management & Trading committed their \"Sea Hazel\" 106/2004 Tsuneishi, Japan (SS 01/2024, DD 06/2025, BWTS fitted) for excess USD 31 mill. For reference, the one-year-older sister vessel \"Oaka\" 106/2003 Tsuneishi, Japan (SS 08/2026, DD 08/2024) was sold back in February at excess USD 24 mill. Gulf Energy Maritime have committed their LR1 \"Gulf Crystal\" 75/2009 Hyundai Mipo, Korea (SS/DD 11/2024, BWTS fitted) to undisclosed buyers for USD 29,5 mill and the older \"Gulf Coast\" Hyundai, Korea (SS 11/2025, DD 12/2023, BWTS fitted), \"Gulf Horizon\" Hyundai, Korea (SS 07/2025, DD 10/2023, BWTS fitted) & \"Gulf Pearl\" Hyundai, Korea (SS 04/2025, DD 07/2023, BWTS fitted) for USD 61,2 mill enbloc.",
    "freight": {
      "Capesize": "at the level of mid usd 8,00's fio range. A number of Indian trips via South Africa into India were reported at the level of usd 17,000/18,000 pd range. No period activity to report here.",
      "Kamsarmax / Panamax": "A number of trips from China into India with metcoke were fixed around usd 7,000/8,000 pd. A number of Indonesian trips into China were reported fixed at the usd 5,000/7,000 pd range. A number of Australian trips into India were fixed around usd 8,000/10,000 pd. South East Asian trips via East Coast South America into China were reported at the level of usd 10,000/11,000 pd. Indian Coastal trips were fixed around usd 10,000/12,000 pd. Inter- Continental trips via US Gulf were reported at the level of usd 10,000/11,000 pd. South American trips into China were reported at the level of usd 15,000/16,000 pd plus ballast bonus at the usd 500K/625K. A Kamsarmax was fixed on period at the usd 15,500 pd basis delivery China for 5/7 months employment.",
      "Ultramax / Supramax": "A number of trips from China into Continent were reported at the level of usd 8,000/9,000 pd. A number of Indonesian trips into China were fixed around usd 7,000/9,000 pd. Indian iron ore trips into China were reported at the level of usd 11,000 pd. South American trips into Continent were fixed around usd 17,000/19,000 pd. South American trips into China were reported at the level of usd 15,000 pd plus ballast bonus at the usd 525K. No period activity to report here.",
      "Handymax / Handysize": "A generally quiet week for this segment. A number of East Coast South American trips into West Coast South America were reported at the level of usd 21,000/22,000 pd. East Coast South American trips US Gulf were fixed around usd 14,000/15,000 pd. No period activity to report here."
    }
  },
